|> Exercise
    handle=_dimensionality_xv_over_c^2_

    If $x$ is a spatial displacement, $v$ is a velocity (speed),
    and $c$ is the speed of light, what is
    the dimension of $xv/c^2$?

    |> Solution

        The factor

        $$
        {v\over c}
        $$

        is dimensionless since $v$ and $c$ both
        have dimensions of speed (speed/speed = 1),
        so

        $$
        {xv\over c^2} = {v\over c}\cdot{x\over c}
        $$

        has the same dimensions as 

        $$
        {x\over c}
        $$

        |> ImageRight
            at-least-as-wide=false
            src=tmp-images/e6_v_over_c_cancellation_cloud.svg
            offset-x=1em

        which has dimensions of time by Exercise >>_dimensionality_t_over_v_.
